"mudmode Materials" means the free mudmode kit files, setup scripts, rules,
templates, adapters and other mudmode materials the Licensor publishes under
this license, including mudmode material shown on mudmodecrew.com.
"Your AI tools" means AI assistants, agents, chat apps and coding tools that
you use for yourself, under your own account or on your own devices,
including online AI services such as chat apps with project files or memory.

1. Personal use. You may read the mudmode Materials and use and privately modify
   them for your own personal, non-commercial setup, free of charge, on devices
   you own or control and in your own accounts with online services (for
   example your AI tools, cloud storage and backups) that only you use.
   "Personal, non-commercial" means use by one individual for their own projects,
   not on behalf of an employer, client or organization and not as part of a
   paid service. Commercial, team and organization use need a separate paid
   license from the Licensor (contact above).
2. No redistribution. Except as section 4 allows, you may not sell, resell,
   share, publish, upload, sublicense, rebrand, or otherwise distribute the
   mudmode Materials, or modified versions, in whole or in part, except forking
   within GitHub as GitHub's Terms of Service allow for public repositories.
   You may share links to the official free download, and short quotes (for
   example to ask for help in the members chat), as long as you don't post
   whole files. Copying the mudmode Materials onto your own devices, into your
   own accounts, into your own backups, or into your own AI tools, as section 4
   describes, is not sharing.
3. No competing copies. You may not publish kits, templates, rule books, guides,
   courses, prompts or datasets that copy the mudmode Materials, or that are
   made by adapting, translating, summarizing or paraphrasing them. This
   doesn't stop you from writing about your own experience, or from publishing
   your own ideas, rules or setups written without copying the mudmode
   Materials.
4. Using the mudmode Materials with AI.
   Allowed (this is what they are for):
   (a) using them with your own AI tools to run your own setup;
   (b) loading them, or any part of them, into your own AI tools'
       instructions, project files, knowledge, memory or search index, for your
       own use under section 1, including uploading files to your own account
       with an online AI service;
   (c) letting your own AI tools, or the kit's own setup scripts, read, copy,
       install and change your copy on your own devices and in your own
       accounts;
   (d) using an AI service in the ordinary way under that service's own terms.
       That is not a breach of this section even if the service's terms let it
       learn from what you upload. Where your AI service offers a setting to
       keep your chats and files out of model training, we ask you to use it
       for mudmode files.
   Not allowed:
   (e) using the mudmode Materials, or knowingly letting them be used, to
       train, fine-tune or evaluate an AI model, or including them in a
       dataset, except as the law allows without permission. Picking an AI
       service or setting for the purpose of getting the mudmode Materials into
       a training set counts as letting them be used;
   (f) feeding them to AI agents or tools to generate competing products, kits,
       rule books, prompts or services (see section 3);
   (g) copying them by automated means (bots, crawlers, scrapers) for anything
       other than the allowed uses above.
   Text-and-data-mining rights are expressly reserved, including under
   Article 4(3) of EU Directive 2019/790.
5. Names and marks. "mudmode" is a trademark of Michael J Hester, used under
