6. Contributions. Lessons, ideas and other contributions are covered by
   CONTRIBUTING.md (and the mudmode lesson terms, where they apply), not by
   this license.
7. Your AI, your decisions.
   (a) You are in charge of your AI tools. You decide what they are allowed to
       do, which permissions and accounts you give them, and whether to accept
       their work. Review what they plan and what they did, especially before
       anything risky or hard to undo (deleting, sending, publishing, paying,
       changing live systems).
   (b) Guidance, not guarantees. The mudmode Materials are rules, templates
       and tools designed to help AI assistants work more safely and steadily.
       They can't control what an AI tool actually does and don't guarantee
       any result. AI tools make mistakes and can take actions you did not
       intend. Setup scripts change files only when you choose to run them;
       read what they will do first and keep backups.
   (c) Third-party AI tools and services (for example Anthropic, xAI, OpenAI,
       GitHub or Gumroad) are run by other companies under their own terms.
       Neither the Licensor nor the Copyright Owner controls them or is
       responsible for their costs or charges, outages or changes, how they
       store or use your data, or the actions they take. You are responsible
       for following their terms and paying their costs.
   (d) mudmode is a way of organizing AI assistants. It is not legal,
       financial, security or professional advice. Results vary.
